Hi team,

Your report grade is 93/100 (the feedback sheet is attached). Overall: a well=
-scoped project with an honest reliability analysis. The decision to move TER=
SE to an automatic feature, and to explain why, was the right call.

Main points:
- The 14 pages are well used. Section 5 is the strongest part of the report.
- -4: the claim that NEG-TUTOR "predicts session abandonment" rests on 31 aba=
ndoned sessions. Call it an association and report the confidence interval.
- -3: the limitations section doesn't discuss that both tutoring deployments =
were in the same university and course level.

If you're planning to turn this into a workshop paper, I'm happy to read a dr=
aft over the summer.

Alan Brooks, Ph.D.
Grado Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering
Virginia Tech

